  "notes": "USAGE:\n{逃亡|とうぼう} implies serious flight — running from the law, escaping persecution, or deserting. It has a heavier tone than {逃|に}げる (to run away) and is common in news reporting.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- から{逃亡|とうぼう}する (to flee from...)\n- へ{逃亡|とうぼう}する (to flee to...)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {逃亡|とうぼう}{生活|せいかつ} (life on the run)\n- {逃亡|とうぼう}{中|ちゅう} (on the run, at large)\n- {逃亡|とうぼう}{者|しゃ} (fugitive)\n- {逃亡|とうぼう}を{図|はか}る (to attempt to flee)\n- {海外|かいがい}に{逃亡|とうぼう}する (to flee abroad)",
